Asset management for small water systems — US EPA (@wu-assets: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_78ZKEFSZ16WYQ5E62DWKR8FP3N
US EPA, Office of Water. Asset Management: A Handbook for Small Water Systems, STEP Guide Series, EPA-816-R-21-006, April 2022. [Official complete text](https://nepis.epa.gov/Exe/ZyPURL.cgi?Dockey=P10154RD.TXT).

Read the whole handbook and work its examples from a stated service level through inventory, priorities, future needs and implementation. Translate its financial worksheets into the actual institution's accounting and price year instead of copying historical figures.

The cover, contents and worksheets were inspected on 30 October 2026. Public access is available; retain agency attribution and any separately credited components. Use the handbook to make inspection, skilled work, spares, replacement and finance visible in a continuing service. A ranked asset list needs physical evidence and an explicit consequence model, not only a spreadsheet score.

